WEBVTT


00:00:27.648 --> 00:00:29.088
The question of happiness


00:00:29.249 --> 00:00:31.213
has preoccupied
philosophers, poets


00:00:31.368 --> 00:00:33.932
and pharmaceutical companies
for thousands of years.


00:00:35.088 --> 00:00:37.608
Clearly, it's a tricky one.


00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:40.528
When I graduated from
design school three years ago,


00:00:40.687 --> 00:00:43.415
I had a definite plan.


00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:47.168
Couple months at home,
put together a kickass portfolio,


00:00:47.327 --> 00:00:50.371
then I'd take Manhattan
by storm.


00:00:52.726 --> 00:00:54.287
And here is home.


00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:56.727
West Orange, New Jersey.


00:00:56.886 --> 00:00:58.491
Nice, huh?


00:01:00.087 --> 00:01:03.207
OK, it's not Manhattan,
but, like I say, it's temporary.


00:01:03.366 --> 00:01:07.130
I grew up here
with two families.


00:01:07.286 --> 00:01:09.970
That's my dad in blue,
and that's his best friend, Terry.


00:01:10.126 --> 00:01:11.970
The Inseparables.


00:01:12.126 --> 00:01:15.214
They go jogging together
three times a week without fail.


00:01:15.365 --> 00:01:17.526
You can set your clock by it.


00:01:17.685 --> 00:01:20.446
You could say life in the Oranges
is dependable.


00:01:20.605 --> 00:01:22.569
I can't believe
you made me do this.


00:01:22.725 --> 00:01:25.453
Good for your appetite.
See you in an hour.


00:01:25.605 --> 00:01:28.693
You can depend on Terry
to have a gadget for everything.


00:01:28.845 --> 00:01:31.572
Walked 1.2 miles.
Only stopped twice.


00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.045
That's great, honey.


00:01:33.204 --> 00:01:35.091
And you can
depend on Cathy


00:01:35.244 --> 00:01:37.044
to never hear
a single word he says.


00:01:37.204 --> 00:01:38.884
Make sure you put your bicycle
in the garage.


00:01:39.044 --> 00:01:40.888
And pull the pork
out of the freezer, honey.


00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:46.251
Across the street,
our house.


00:01:46.404 --> 00:01:48.771
Every year,
my mom gets more involved


00:01:48.924 --> 00:01:50.287
with her carolling group.


00:01:50.444 --> 00:01:52.244
They start rehearsing
in August.


00:01:52.403 --> 00:01:53.963
# Jingle bells
Jingle all the way... #


00:01:54.123 --> 00:01:56.688
And every year, my dad
hates them a little bit more.


00:01:59.723 --> 00:02:03.564
OK, sure. I'm still here.
I'm a few years behind in my plan.


00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.490
But you can't
rush these things.


00:02:05.643 --> 00:02:08.491
Portfolios need
to be perfect, right?


00:02:08.642 --> 00:02:11.282
Plus I have a day job
working in furniture, so...


00:02:11.442 --> 00:02:14.802
...as far as I was concerned,
everything was on track.


00:02:14.962 --> 00:02:18.006
# Happy birthday to you... #


00:02:18.161 --> 00:02:21.009
That is, until what
happened... happened


00:02:21.162 --> 00:02:23.246
Nina Ostroff.


00:02:23.401 --> 00:02:26.085
When all this started,
she was at a safe distance,


00:02:26.241 --> 00:02:28.281
3, 000 miles away
in San Francisco.


00:02:28.441 --> 00:02:32.085
I Happy birthday to you. I


00:02:32.241 --> 00:02:34.565
Make a wish, babe.


00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.208
And I was the fifth wheel


00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.608
to our parents'
regular Saturday foursome.


00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:48.440
Say it again.


00:02:48.599 --> 00:02:49.887
OK.


00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.363
Un coup de birch.


00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.003
Hey, Vanny.


00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:55.643
I read the most
interesting article


00:02:55.799 --> 00:02:57.567
called 'The IKEA Conspiracy',


00:02:57.719 --> 00:02:59.324
which you'd be
really fascinated by.


00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:00.800
- What it imagines is a...
- Terry?


00:03:00.959 --> 00:03:02.442
We need to call Nina.
We said 9:30.


00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:04.039
I'm on it.


00:03:04.199 --> 00:03:06.403
Vanessa, did you look at
that one-bedroom in Fort Lee?


00:03:06.558 --> 00:03:09.723
Yeah. It was, um, like a closet
in the basement.


00:03:09.878 --> 00:03:11.242
There's always something, honey.


00:03:11.398 --> 00:03:12.719
Don't be so choosy.
Nothing's perfect.


00:03:12.878 --> 00:03:15.039
There was, you know,
one window.


00:03:15.198 --> 00:03:17.042
- Paige, did I tell you...
- No room to breathe.


00:03:17.198 --> 00:03:18.878
...that Joan Marshack
was the listing agent on that?


00:03:19.038 --> 00:03:21.842
David, you are going
to really love this.


00:03:21.998 --> 00:03:26.799
This speaker box communicates
wirelessly with my cell phone.


00:03:26.958 --> 00:03:29.042
And guess where
I read about it first.


00:03:29.197 --> 00:03:31.205
'Consumer Reports'. Thank you
so much for the subscription.


00:03:31.358 --> 00:03:33.606
- I'm really enjoying it.
- You are consumingly welcome.


00:03:33.757 --> 00:03:36.845
I don't even have to take
my cell phone out of my pocket.


00:03:36.997 --> 00:03:38.318
Watch.


00:03:38.477 --> 00:03:40.321
Dial Nina.


00:03:40.477 --> 00:03:41.917
Please repeat request.


00:03:42.076 --> 00:03:43.397
Dial Nina.


00:03:43.557 --> 00:03:45.641
Maybe your pants
are blocking the signal.


00:03:45.796 --> 00:03:47.236
They're cotton.


00:03:48.676 --> 00:03:51.316
Nina's cell phone, dialling.


00:03:53.116 --> 00:03:56.117
Nina - their daughter
and my best friend


00:03:56.276 --> 00:03:58.284
from ages 0
to high school.


00:03:58.436 --> 00:04:00.836
We spent hours together
planning our big escape.


00:04:00.996 --> 00:04:02.960
I'm gonna live in New York.


00:04:03.115 --> 00:04:04.436
And Paris.


00:04:04.595 --> 00:04:06.843
And I'm gonna be a famous chef
and have a million lovers


00:04:06.995 --> 00:04:08.316
who'll take me
all over the world


00:04:08.475 --> 00:04:10.603
so I never have to come back
to New Jersey again.


00:04:10.755 --> 00:04:13.482
It's like
there's no air here, right?


00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:15.239
Totally.


00:04:17.914 --> 00:04:19.355
You'll come too, right?


00:04:19.514 --> 00:04:21.434
Are you kidding?


00:04:22.635 --> 00:04:24.402
Until sophomore year,


00:04:24.554 --> 00:04:28.842
when she abandoned me for
Liz Gaines and the Fun Bunch.


00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:35.634
She also kissed and later gave
a hand job to Peter Fortunate.


00:04:35.794 --> 00:04:38.914
I'd been secretly
in love with him forever.


00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:41.997
Then, just as her parents
were lining her up


00:04:42.153 --> 00:04:43.953
at some lame college
in Pennsylvania,


00:04:44.113 --> 00:04:46.557
she decided she was
going to travel the world.


00:04:46.713 --> 00:04:49.157
Or at least those parts


00:04:49.312 --> 00:04:51.232
that were out of
her mothefs cell phone range.


00:04:54.632 --> 00:04:56.279
Hello?


00:04:56.432 --> 00:04:58.832
Happy birthday, sweetie!


00:04:58.992 --> 00:05:00.640
- Happy birthday!
- Happy birthday, Nina.


00:05:00.792 --> 00:05:03.640
It's David and Paige.
Vanessa's here too.


00:05:03.792 --> 00:05:05.516
It's true. I'm here.


00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:06.960
Hey, Ethan.


00:05:07.111 --> 00:05:09.839
I think Nina's fucking parents
are on the phone.


00:05:11.592 --> 00:05:14.036
I didn't know I was having
a party. It was a surprise.


00:05:14.191 --> 00:05:16.275
Honey, we can't hear you.


00:05:16.431 --> 00:05:19.038
Ethan threw me
a surprise party.


00:05:19.191 --> 00:05:20.915
It's so great.


00:05:21.071 --> 00:05:22.392
Did you guys get
the pictures I sent?


00:05:22.551 --> 00:05:24.275
Yes, we did.


00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:26.111
More young men should have earrings
in their face.


00:05:26.271 --> 00:05:28.671
What? I'm sorry, I can't
hear you. Am I on speaker?


00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:32.551
Nina, what day are you
flying in for Thanksgiving?


00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:35.754
Thanksgiving. Mom, um...


00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.754
Uh, I don't think I'm gonna
make it for Thanksgiving.


00:05:39.909 --> 00:05:43.030
Ethan's photography show's
next weekend, and it's a big deal.


00:05:43.189 --> 00:05:44.989
Sweetie, we haven't
seen you for two years.


00:05:45.149 --> 00:05:46.513
You haven't been home
in five years.


00:05:46.669 --> 00:05:48.394
Since we visited you.
That's a long time.


00:05:48.549 --> 00:05:49.869
Um...


00:05:50.029 --> 00:05:52.037
Can you take me
off speaker, please?


00:05:52.189 --> 00:05:53.630
Sorry, sweetie,
I'd have to disconnect you


00:05:53.789 --> 00:05:55.753
to take you off speaker -
it's a very complex system.


00:05:55.909 --> 00:05:56.913
OK.


00:05:58.308 --> 00:06:01.157
Look, you're not
gonna like this, but...


00:06:01.308 --> 00:06:03.392
Ethan and I
are getting married.


00:06:03.548 --> 00:06:06.669
He proposed two weeks ago
on his birthday.


00:06:06.828 --> 00:06:08.432
He took me out
to Baker Beach,


00:06:08.588 --> 00:06:09.908
which overlooks
the Golden Gate Bridge,


00:06:10.068 --> 00:06:11.912
and he got down on one knee
and everything.


00:06:12.068 --> 00:06:15.472
- He proposed on his birthday?
- I don't understand.


00:06:15.628 --> 00:06:17.395
I'm in love with him.


00:06:18.388 --> 00:06:20.396
That's really great,
sweetie, but...


00:06:20.547 --> 00:06:22.588
You're only 24 years old.


00:06:22.747 --> 00:06:24.591
Nobody gets married
at 24 anymore.


00:06:24.747 --> 00:06:26.591
People get married
when they're 17.


00:06:26.747 --> 00:06:28.111
Not white girls
from New Jersey.


00:06:28.267 --> 00:06:29.827
- Shh!
- Would you listen to yourself?


00:06:29.987 --> 00:06:31.591
No, you listen -
you have made some


00:06:31.746 --> 00:06:33.950
very questionable decisions
in your life.


00:06:34.106 --> 00:06:35.470
Please don't
add to the list


00:06:35.626 --> 00:06:39.315
by marrying some loser kid
with zero future.


00:06:39.466 --> 00:06:42.434
OK. I have an idea.


00:06:42.586 --> 00:06:46.634
If you think he's such a loser,
then don't come to the wedding!


00:06:51.065 --> 00:06:52.745
Jesus, turn that thing down!


00:06:55.105 --> 00:06:59.546
Down volume!
Down volume!


00:06:59.705 --> 00:07:02.945
- Oh, God!
- Down volume!


00:07:08.865 --> 00:07:12.105
You guys, it's getting late.
The party's over, OK?


00:07:12.264 --> 00:07:14.032
Love you. 'Bye.


00:07:14.184 --> 00:07:15.668
Amy, did you see Ethan?


00:07:16.824 --> 00:07:18.265
Baby?


00:07:18.424 --> 00:07:20.584
Ethan?


00:07:24.543 --> 00:07:25.951
Ethan?


00:07:26.103 --> 00:07:28.427
Uh, it's...
Gimme a sec.


00:07:28.583 --> 00:07:30.951
Come on. I want to
get everybody out of here.


00:07:45.222 --> 00:07:47.262
Hey, how's it going with
the, uh, couples counsellor?


00:07:47.422 --> 00:07:49.986
I don't know.
She's so non-specific.


00:07:50.142 --> 00:07:52.782
It's like talking to fog.


00:07:52.942 --> 00:07:55.102
David and I know
where we stand with each other.


00:07:55.261 --> 00:07:57.629
That's how we've lasted this long.
Somehow, it works.


00:07:57.782 --> 00:08:01.306
Well, don't look at me.
I just pretend Terry's invisible.


00:08:01.461 --> 00:08:03.981
- Notice anything different?
- I sure do.


00:08:04.141 --> 00:08:05.865
Nice new mini fridge.


00:08:06.021 --> 00:08:07.462
I think it really
ties the room together.


00:08:07.621 --> 00:08:10.065
-It's the Max 5950.
-It's the one you recommended.


00:08:10.221 --> 00:08:12.108
From the patio series.
Good move.


00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:14.301
Let's take a look
in the mini ice compartment.


00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:17.500
Oh, boy.
It's really big, isn't it?


00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.748
Now, this stuff is huge
in Europe.


00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:23.387
And we've just landed
the American campaign.


00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:25.100
- No kidding? Congrats.
- Thanks.


00:08:25.259 --> 00:08:27.267
Russians like it
for breakfast.


00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:31.667
Before the devil
knows you're dead.


00:08:35.019 --> 00:08:36.786
Boy, it's, um...


00:08:36.939 --> 00:08:38.466
Well...
Really not very good, is it?


00:08:38.619 --> 00:08:40.463
-It's not good at all. No.
- No.


00:08:46.059 --> 00:08:47.542
What's up
with these sheets?


00:08:48.858 --> 00:08:50.899
You, um...


00:08:51.058 --> 00:08:52.858
...spending a little extra time
out here?


00:08:53.018 --> 00:08:55.179
Just a couple of nights a week.


00:08:55.338 --> 00:08:57.706
Late-night TV.


00:09:21.617 --> 00:09:24.421
You've gotta be
fucking kidding me.


00:09:31.416 --> 00:09:33.456
Oh, sh...


00:09:45.775 --> 00:09:47.302
Nina? Wow!


00:09:47.455 --> 00:09:50.259
- David. Hi.
- It's been so long.


00:09:51.694 --> 00:09:54.455
I thought you weren't
coming back for Thanksgiving.


00:09:54.615 --> 00:09:56.502
Yeah, well...


00:09:56.654 --> 00:09:58.422
Um...


00:09:59.974 --> 00:10:03.139
Are my parents here?
Locked out.


00:10:03.294 --> 00:10:05.542
They're in the back.


00:10:05.694 --> 00:10:08.334
Last day of barbecue season.


00:10:10.773 --> 00:10:13.054
What's going on?


00:10:13.213 --> 00:10:14.817
- You OK?
- David?


00:10:14.973 --> 00:10:17.373
Paige wants to know what
you did with the tong thing.


00:10:18.773 --> 00:10:20.453
Hi, Mom.


00:10:20.613 --> 00:10:23.733
I'm back for Thanksgiving.


00:10:23.892 --> 00:10:26.053
We turned it into
a second den.


00:10:26.212 --> 00:10:27.860
If your father's
in the first den


00:10:28.012 --> 00:10:29.572
and I want some privacy,
I come here.


00:10:29.733 --> 00:10:31.096
Honey,
I have this really cool


00:10:31.253 --> 00:10:32.573
self-inflating mattress.


00:10:32.732 --> 00:10:35.297
It fits perfectly in the corner
and it is really comfy.


00:10:37.692 --> 00:10:40.180
But, you know, we have your
old bed frame out there in the...


00:10:40.332 --> 00:10:42.219
...in the garage -
I can set it up for you.


00:10:42.372 --> 00:10:44.500
- Take me two...two se...
- No, that's fine.


00:10:44.651 --> 00:10:46.571
I'll only be here
a few days.


00:10:46.731 --> 00:10:49.176
Why? Where are you
going to now?


00:10:49.331 --> 00:10:51.776
I don't know.


00:10:53.531 --> 00:10:55.451
I haven't figured it out yet.


00:10:55.611 --> 00:10:57.498
Well, why don't you
stay here for a while?


00:10:57.650 --> 00:10:59.091
I don't care -
it's not like we haven't


00:10:59.251 --> 00:11:01.412
gotten used
to you being gone.


00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:04.010
Can you hold off
on the guilt trips


00:11:04.171 --> 00:11:05.491
for just a little while,
please?


00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:07.211
I've had
a rough couple days.


00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:11.730
I'd never seen Nina
with her tail between her legs.


00:11:11.889 --> 00:11:14.530
But I didn't
have time to gloat.


00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:17.734
Back on our side of the street,
we had our own problems.


00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:19.254
That's not what I'm saying.


00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:21.374
- What about Christmas?
- Come on, Paige.


00:11:21.529 --> 00:11:24.650
- I'm trying here.
- Oh. Now I'm not trying.


00:11:25.889 --> 00:11:27.536
Can't we have
a simple conversation?


00:11:27.689 --> 00:11:31.573
- I make one suggestion...
- I don't want to go down there.


00:11:31.729 --> 00:11:34.490
- You seem oblivious...
- Come on, Paige...


00:11:41.488 --> 00:11:43.736
I apologise
for what I said about Ethan.


00:11:43.888 --> 00:11:46.649
- Were you waiting for me?
- I'm not your enemy. Nina!


00:11:46.808 --> 00:11:48.292
When you're a parent
some day,


00:11:48.448 --> 00:11:49.856
you'll understand
what it feels like


00:11:50.007 --> 00:11:51.807
to have your child hate you.


00:11:52.848 --> 00:11:54.735
In case you're wondering,
that's your cue to say,


00:11:54.887 --> 00:11:56.208
"I don't hate you, Mom."


00:11:56.367 --> 00:11:57.775
I don't hate you.


00:11:57.927 --> 00:12:02.652
I just get furious
thinking someone has hurt you.


00:12:06.287 --> 00:12:09.691
Don't think I'm crazy.
This is just a thought. But, uh...


00:12:11.087 --> 00:12:13.454
Toby's coming home
for Thanksgiving.


00:12:15.206 --> 00:12:17.727
- Oh, my God.
- He's gotten very attractive.


00:12:17.886 --> 00:12:19.249
That's all I'm saying.


00:12:19.406 --> 00:12:21.326
He works for
the Federal Trade Commission.


00:12:21.486 --> 00:12:22.849
Terrific. You date him.


00:12:23.006 --> 00:12:24.806
Well, it's not like you two
don't have history.


00:12:24.966 --> 00:12:26.494
- We kissed!
- Yeah.


00:12:26.645 --> 00:12:27.966
Once, like, 10 years ago.


00:12:28.125 --> 00:12:30.569
Can you at least let me unpack
before pimping me out?


00:12:30.726 --> 00:12:33.410
OK, fine. But I'm gonna
tell you this for your own good.


00:12:33.565 --> 00:12:36.369
You need to have a real
relationship with a real man.


00:12:36.525 --> 00:12:38.969
It's time you grew up already!
Stop running away.


00:12:39.124 --> 00:12:42.125
You know, you're right.
I'm being selfish.


00:12:42.284 --> 00:12:43.725
The best thing
I can do right now


00:12:43.885 --> 00:12:45.205
is fulfil
your insane suburban fantasy


00:12:45.364 --> 00:12:46.685
where I marry
your best friend's son.


00:12:46.844 --> 00:12:50.249
Now, you go call the catering hall
and I'll lube my vagina.


00:12:50.404 --> 00:12:52.848
That was uncalled for.


00:12:53.004 --> 00:12:54.487
Uh, there's 12 of us
in the delegation.


00:12:54.644 --> 00:12:56.204
I'm really just...
just assisting my boss.


00:12:56.364 --> 00:12:58.328
But the goal is to
tie our trade agreements


00:12:58.483 --> 00:13:00.251
to stricter
environmental regulations


00:13:00.403 --> 00:13:02.531
since things
are kind of a mess over there.


00:13:03.923 --> 00:13:06.487
- China. That's great.
- Yeah, thanks.


00:13:06.643 --> 00:13:08.443
You are gonna have
a great experience.


00:13:08.603 --> 00:13:10.926
- Yeah. Yeah.
- It's, like, a 30-hour flight.


00:13:11.083 --> 00:13:13.123
- Honey, what about Christmas?
- Don't worry, Mom.


00:13:13.282 --> 00:13:14.603
I fly back on the 24th.


00:13:14.762 --> 00:13:16.290
That sounds
really great, Toby.


00:13:16.442 --> 00:13:19.203
I hear that ultimate frisbee
is exploding over there.


00:13:19.362 --> 00:13:21.446
In China. The, uh...


00:13:21.603 --> 00:13:25.084
The Beijing club team
came in second at the World's.


00:13:25.242 --> 00:13:26.846
If I see a game,
I'll let 'em know


00:13:27.002 --> 00:13:30.045
I grew up across the street
from the guy who invented it.


00:13:30.202 --> 00:13:33.770
Well. It wasn't just me. It was
also Jared Kass and, uh...


00:13:33.922 --> 00:13:35.569
- Honey?
- Joel Silver.


00:13:35.722 --> 00:13:37.326
Of course, Joel gets
most of the, you know...


00:13:37.481 --> 00:13:40.166
...most of the play, being
a big movie producer and all.


00:13:40.321 --> 00:13:42.569
Finally!


00:13:45.001 --> 00:13:47.129
Where there's dessert,
there's hope.


00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:54.521
Your mom told me about what
happened with that Ethan guy.


00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:56.600
You OK?


00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:01.400
Yeah.


00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:03.688
I'm good, thanks.


00:14:04.999 --> 00:14:06.919
So, what about you?


00:14:07.079 --> 00:14:09.088
How's the liquor
advertising business going?


00:14:09.239 --> 00:14:11.007
Still pushing booze
onto minors?


00:14:11.159 --> 00:14:13.603
Yes, I am.


00:14:13.759 --> 00:14:15.079
Actually,
I just got a promotion.


00:14:15.239 --> 00:14:16.766
I'm now executive
vice-president,


00:14:16.919 --> 00:14:18.239
creative accounts.


00:14:18.398 --> 00:14:19.926
Congratulations.


00:14:20.079 --> 00:14:22.207
Was that something
you wanted?


00:14:22.358 --> 00:14:24.399
Not really.


00:14:24.558 --> 00:14:26.478
You want me to spoon this
onto the plates?


00:14:26.638 --> 00:14:28.122
Please.


00:14:28.278 --> 00:14:31.759
Uh... Don't just eat it
right out the carton.


00:14:34.478 --> 00:14:37.358
Is it good?


00:14:39.557 --> 00:14:40.965
- It's cold.
- What?


00:14:41.118 --> 00:14:45.122
Hey. I brought that ice-cream
for the pies.


00:14:45.277 --> 00:14:47.164
He made me eat it.


00:14:48.397 --> 00:14:50.165
Well, Cathy wants
to serve dessert.


00:14:50.317 --> 00:14:52.085
Will you please
bring in some plates?


00:14:54.356 --> 00:14:56.724
I still need Christmas lists
from everyone by tonight.


00:14:56.877 --> 00:14:58.197
I'm leaving early tomorrow.


00:14:58.356 --> 00:15:00.364
- Black Friday.
- Don't make fun.


00:15:00.516 --> 00:15:04.324
Last year, I got there at 3am
and I was still 210 in line.


00:15:04.476 --> 00:15:05.916
Why would anyone
want to shop


00:15:06.076 --> 00:15:07.681
on the same day
as everyone else?


00:15:07.836 --> 00:15:09.756
I hear that
they have fist fights


00:15:09.916 --> 00:15:11.640
and people throw their children
at each other.


00:15:11.796 --> 00:15:14.644
Terry! No.
It's really a very...


00:15:14.795 --> 00:15:18.679
Very communal, Christmassy
experience. It's beautiful.


00:15:18.835 --> 00:15:20.199
Listen, I know it's late,


00:15:20.355 --> 00:15:21.839
but I think
we should have a toast.


00:15:21.995 --> 00:15:24.363
It's Thanksgiving. We have
so much to be thankful for.


00:15:24.515 --> 00:15:26.675
Toby is going to China.


00:15:26.834 --> 00:15:28.155
Very exciting.


00:15:28.315 --> 00:15:30.879
Nina is finally
back at home.


00:15:31.035 --> 00:15:33.796
And Vanessa
continues to live among us,


00:15:33.954 --> 00:15:35.634
bringing us joy every day.


00:15:35.794 --> 00:15:37.681
To the Walling
and Ostroff clans.


00:15:37.834 --> 00:15:41.402
Who knew that two families
could get this close?


00:15:41.554 --> 00:15:42.874
Hear, hear.


00:15:43.033 --> 00:15:45.598
I still think we could be
a little closer.


00:15:47.593 --> 00:15:49.874
Well said.


00:15:51.913 --> 00:15:55.001
Man, I thought your mom
was going to applaud


00:15:55.153 --> 00:15:56.474
when she saw us
leave together.


00:15:56.633 --> 00:15:59.481
The woman
is a total lunatic.


00:15:59.633 --> 00:16:01.477
In the first three years
I was gone,


00:16:01.633 --> 00:16:03.433
she sent me
letters from the cat.


00:16:03.592 --> 00:16:05.840
"Dear Nina,
Don't be difficult.


00:16:05.993 --> 00:16:07.400
"Call your mother
on her birthday."


00:16:07.552 --> 00:16:09.920
That's great, actually.
I kind of like that.


00:16:10.072 --> 00:16:12.560
Now you understand
why I never came back.


00:16:13.592 --> 00:16:15.675
Yeah. No, I hear ya. But...


00:16:15.832 --> 00:16:18.352
I'm glad you did.


00:16:19.671 --> 00:16:20.719
Shut up.


00:16:24.871 --> 00:16:26.595
Dance with me.


00:16:28.231 --> 00:16:29.715
Totally.


00:16:33.391 --> 00:16:34.951
You OK?


00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:36.431
I need to get some water.


00:16:36.591 --> 00:16:38.478
- Can I get some water?
- OK. Sit down, wild man.


00:16:38.631 --> 00:16:42.112
I'm sorry.
I'm so sorry.


00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:48.954
- Hey.
- Toby needs water.


00:16:49.109 --> 00:16:50.877
What are you doing up?


00:16:51.029 --> 00:16:54.237
Just watching a little TV
in the man cave.


00:16:54.390 --> 00:16:57.510
- Man cave?
- It's the pool house.


00:16:57.669 --> 00:17:00.430
I got one of those
worldwide sports...


00:17:00.589 --> 00:17:02.717
...something something package
your dad recommended.


00:17:02.869 --> 00:17:05.073
There's this
Korean basketball league


00:17:05.229 --> 00:17:06.876
which is completely crazy.


00:17:07.029 --> 00:17:09.157
You know, it's not good
to eat peanut butter


00:17:09.308 --> 00:17:10.629
this late at night.


00:17:10.788 --> 00:17:12.109
It'll make you fat.


00:17:12.268 --> 00:17:14.112
I'm not fat.


00:17:14.268 --> 00:17:15.993
You will be if you
keep eating like that


00:17:16.148 --> 00:17:17.468
at 2:00 in the morning.


00:17:17.628 --> 00:17:19.275
And where'd you pick
this little factoid up?


00:17:19.428 --> 00:17:21.032
I worked in
a lot of restaurants.


00:17:21.187 --> 00:17:23.315
Restaurants
that serve peanut butter?


00:17:23.468 --> 00:17:25.476
Look, do whatever you want.


00:17:25.628 --> 00:17:28.072
I'm just saying
that you wouldn't look good fat.


00:17:30.547 --> 00:17:32.434
I should get back downstairs.


00:17:32.587 --> 00:17:34.354
Yeah, make your mother
very happy. You know that.


00:17:34.507 --> 00:17:35.827
It's what I live for.


00:18:23.224 --> 00:18:25.144
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:18:26.344 --> 00:18:27.871
What happened to Toby?


00:18:28.024 --> 00:18:29.944
I cut him up
in little pieces


00:18:30.104 --> 00:18:31.904
and put him in the fridge
for later.


00:18:39.103 --> 00:18:40.663
Who's playing?


00:18:42.263 --> 00:18:44.107
I have no idea.


00:18:44.263 --> 00:18:46.107
It's...it's the, um...


00:18:48.463 --> 00:18:50.546
...guys in red against the...
the guys in white.


00:18:50.703 --> 00:18:52.350
- White. I got it.
- Yeah. Yeah.


00:18:52.503 --> 00:18:54.511
Go, reds.


00:18:54.662 --> 00:18:56.343
Or White.


00:18:56.502 --> 00:18:58.182
You know.


00:19:41.899 --> 00:19:43.907
Oh, fuck.


00:19:46.899 --> 00:19:50.227
One bedroom, high ceilings.
Close to the PATH train.


00:19:50.379 --> 00:19:52.179
Ooh, washer dryer.


00:19:52.339 --> 00:19:54.903
- Plus it's crazy bright.
- Yeah.


00:19:55.058 --> 00:19:57.623
Well, that's morning light.


00:19:57.779 --> 00:19:59.623
I don't want that.


00:19:59.778 --> 00:20:02.627
Wow, that's, like,
your best excuse in two weeks.


00:20:02.778 --> 00:20:04.338
Hello, Koosers.


00:20:04.499 --> 00:20:06.418
- Did you sell that dresser?
- I did not.


00:20:06.578 --> 00:20:08.018
She's not interested
in the apartment, Henry.


00:20:08.178 --> 00:20:09.499
I told you.


00:20:09.658 --> 00:20:11.186
What?


00:20:11.338 --> 00:20:12.942
What do you mean,
"I told you"?


00:20:13.098 --> 00:20:15.782
You've been talking about
moving out for two years.


00:20:15.937 --> 00:20:17.705
You know what?
I'm saving money. Alright?


00:20:17.857 --> 00:20:19.865
I have a very definite plan.


00:20:20.017 --> 00:20:22.221
You mean that "stay at home,
corrode your soul" plan?


00:20:22.377 --> 00:20:24.341
No, no - the plan
where I move to the city


00:20:24.497 --> 00:20:25.981
and I work with
a big designer.


00:20:26.137 --> 00:20:28.265
I've already made
serious contacts.


00:20:28.417 --> 00:20:30.261
From where'?


00:20:30.417 --> 00:20:35.698
Huffman Koos? Well, you know me
and her and Marlon.


00:20:35.856 --> 00:20:38.541
Hey, I'm serious.
We're worried about you.


00:20:38.696 --> 00:20:40.856
OK, thank you.
I got it under control.


00:20:41.016 --> 00:20:42.543
You guys
go worry about yourselves.


00:20:45.496 --> 00:20:47.296
Wow. There she is'


00:20:47.455 --> 00:20:50.663
1 pm. Very impressive.


00:20:50.816 --> 00:20:53.096
So? Did you have fun
last night?


00:20:53.255 --> 00:20:54.935
I'm sure you'd love
a full report.


00:20:55.095 --> 00:20:57.104
You know,
some mothers and daughters


00:20:57.255 --> 00:20:59.895
actually talk about
these things, like friends.


00:21:00.054 --> 00:21:02.182
It's not happening.


00:21:02.335 --> 00:21:06.143
Well, maybe Toby will be
better company than you.


00:21:06.294 --> 00:21:07.702
Hi!


00:21:14.094 --> 00:21:15.818
Try and control yourself.


00:21:20.493 --> 00:21:21.737
Hey, Nina.


00:21:21.893 --> 00:21:24.937
- Morning, Cathy.
- Good morning, Tobias.


00:21:25.093 --> 00:21:27.734
- Uh, you forgot your sweater.
- Thank you.


00:21:27.893 --> 00:21:29.693
Can I get you
some breakfast, honey?


00:21:29.853 --> 00:21:32.057
No, thanks. I'm OK. Thanks.


00:21:33.532 --> 00:21:35.541
Well, I'll give you two
some privacy.


00:21:35.693 --> 00:21:38.420
There you are.


00:21:41.733 --> 00:21:43.533
I can hear you
hovering out there!


00:21:43.692 --> 00:21:45.220
Fine.


00:21:46.532 --> 00:21:48.213
You're looking a little crispy
this morning.


00:21:48.372 --> 00:21:50.413
Oh, thank you.
You can really put 'em away.


00:21:50.572 --> 00:21:53.333
Did I, uh...
Did I pass out?


00:21:53.492 --> 00:21:55.336
Yeah. Mmm, pretty much.


00:21:55.491 --> 00:21:57.695
Sorry about that.


00:21:57.851 --> 00:22:00.372
- No.
- Um...


00:22:01.531 --> 00:22:03.331
Look.
Uh, I was thinking.


00:22:03.491 --> 00:22:07.900
I had a really fun time last night
before passing out, and...


00:22:08.051 --> 00:22:10.179
...I'm supposed to have dinner
with my folks tonight.


00:22:10.331 --> 00:22:13.015
And being as
I'm leaving in two days,


00:22:13.170 --> 00:22:17.731
I thought, you know,
maybe you'd like to join us


00:22:17.890 --> 00:22:20.018
so we could
hang out more.


00:22:20.170 --> 00:22:25.134
Yeah. Dinner with you and
your parents, it...sounds great.


00:22:30.169 --> 00:22:32.373
- Come on, Toby.
- Hold.


00:22:34.209 --> 00:22:35.857
Alright. OK.


00:22:36.009 --> 00:22:37.929
- Let's go, Toby.
- Hold.


00:22:38.089 --> 00:22:41.778
Toby, it's called
the fast-moving tile game.


00:22:41.929 --> 00:22:43.849
Hold.


00:22:46.689 --> 00:22:48.576
- Let's go, Toby.
- Hold!


00:22:48.728 --> 00:22:51.096
OK. OK.


00:22:51.249 --> 00:22:52.896
Actually,
just go out ahead of me.


00:22:53.048 --> 00:22:54.772
Oh!


00:22:54.928 --> 00:22:57.448
5, the 13. I'm out!


00:22:57.608 --> 00:23:00.215
- What?
- Ah. Yes.


00:23:00.368 --> 00:23:01.928
Now, who's gonna help me
with the dishes?


00:23:02.088 --> 00:23:03.571
I will, Mom. Wait.


00:23:03.728 --> 00:23:05.648
Hang on a sec.
I gotta take this. It's work.


00:23:05.807 --> 00:23:07.367
This is Toby.


00:23:07.527 --> 00:23:09.011
Oh, hello, sir.


00:23:09.167 --> 00:23:10.488
Uh-huh.


00:23:10.647 --> 00:23:11.967
- No, no, it's no problem.
- Yeah.


00:23:12.127 --> 00:23:13.807
I think maybe
I'll go pick up a movie


00:23:13.967 --> 00:23:15.450
in case you want to
watch something later.


00:23:15.607 --> 00:23:18.411
- That sounds fun.
- I'll come with you.


00:23:18.566 --> 00:23:21.174
Keep you company
while Toby does the dishes.


00:23:31.766 --> 00:23:33.129
Look.


00:23:33.286 --> 00:23:36.329
What happened last night
was a mistake.


00:23:36.486 --> 00:23:38.734
- OK?
- No, you're right.


00:23:41.485 --> 00:23:44.650
Relax, OK?
It was nothing.


00:23:44.805 --> 00:23:47.009
And you stopped it.
You're absolved.


00:23:57.324 --> 00:23:58.972
Hello in there?


00:23:59.124 --> 00:24:00.685
Is there anyone in there?


00:24:00.844 --> 00:24:03.768
You just have to
instigate trouble.


00:24:03.924 --> 00:24:06.728
I do not instigate trouble.


00:24:06.884 --> 00:24:08.204
Well, OK.


00:24:08.363 --> 00:24:09.891
Well, then, Why'd you
come to dinner tonight?


00:24:10.043 --> 00:24:11.364
Toby invited me.


00:24:11.523 --> 00:24:13.291
And now that we're
talking about instigators,


00:24:13.443 --> 00:24:15.287
you leaned into me.


00:24:15.443 --> 00:24:17.004
I leaned into you?


00:24:17.163 --> 00:24:19.007
- I leaned... I did not lean.
- Yes, you did.


00:24:19.163 --> 00:24:20.724
- You leaned into me.
- What?!


00:24:20.883 --> 00:24:22.891
Oh... He said, she said.


00:24:24.562 --> 00:24:25.883
He said, she said.


00:24:26.042 --> 00:24:27.722
Where did that come from?


00:24:27.882 --> 00:24:29.802
I have no idea
where that came from.


00:24:36.002 --> 00:24:37.846
I'm not instigating.


00:25:03.280 --> 00:25:04.644
I've been thinking
about getting


00:25:04.800 --> 00:25:06.809
one of those
giant electric snow globes.


00:25:06.960 --> 00:25:10.004
You ever seen one of those?
Really big ones?


00:25:10.160 --> 00:25:12.168
Fantastic.


00:25:12.320 --> 00:25:14.284
Mom?


00:25:14.439 --> 00:25:16.523
We're in here, honey.


00:25:16.679 --> 00:25:19.167
I'm going out.


00:25:19.319 --> 00:25:21.403
Well!


00:25:21.560 --> 00:25:24.080
Well, don't you look nice?


00:25:24.239 --> 00:25:25.767
Thanks.


00:25:25.919 --> 00:25:27.360
So is Toby
taking you somewhere?


00:25:27.519 --> 00:25:30.280
- Uh, yeah.
- OK. OK.


00:25:30.439 --> 00:25:31.803
- Fine.
- Mom!


00:25:31.959 --> 00:25:33.683
Give me some room.


00:25:33.838 --> 00:25:36.119
Fine. Have fun.


00:25:40.038 --> 00:25:41.643
Is she eating with us?


00:25:41.798 --> 00:25:44.679
Toby is taking her out.
She was all dressed up.


00:25:44.838 --> 00:25:46.562
- Toby already left for DC.
- What?


00:25:46.718 --> 00:25:48.125
Yeah, first thing
this morning.


00:25:48.278 --> 00:25:50.122
Some congressman wanted
to be with the delegation


00:25:50.277 --> 00:25:51.838
before they went to China.


00:26:21.316 --> 00:26:24.316
"Left this morning."
Oh, shit!


00:26:36.474 --> 00:26:38.558
- H-hello?
- Mom?


00:26:38.715 --> 00:26:40.723
Listen. I lied earlier.


00:26:40.874 --> 00:26:42.642
I'm not going out with Toby.


00:26:42.794 --> 00:26:44.518
He actually left for Washington
this morning.


00:26:44.674 --> 00:26:47.401
- Oh?
- Yeah.


00:26:47.554 --> 00:26:51.721
I'm meeting Meredith Lovett.
Remember her?


00:26:51.874 --> 00:26:54.197
I didn't tell you because
I know you don't like her.


00:26:54.354 --> 00:26:58.402
Oh, honey, thank you.
Thank you for telling me.


00:26:58.553 --> 00:27:02.361
You know...
You don't have to lie to me.


00:27:02.513 --> 00:27:04.554
I know.


00:27:04.713 --> 00:27:06.437
So where are you going?


00:27:08.033 --> 00:27:11.241
Uh, we're going to the Regal
to see a movie.


00:27:13.232 --> 00:27:14.553
Uh, Mom?


00:27:14.712 --> 00:27:17.232
Thanks...for being so cool


00:27:17.392 --> 00:27:19.640
and letting me come back
and stay and everything.


00:27:19.792 --> 00:27:22.640
I've been feeling really
tossed around lately, so...


00:27:22.791 --> 00:27:26.196
You know.
Thanks for being there.


00:27:27.672 --> 00:27:30.072
OK, well...
I'll see you later for dinner.


00:27:35.031 --> 00:27:36.591
Oh, my...


00:28:13.429 --> 00:28:14.673
Whoa!


00:28:14.829 --> 00:28:16.870
Cathy.


00:28:17.029 --> 00:28:19.232
- What are you...?
- I'm, uh...


00:28:19.389 --> 00:28:21.833
- What are you...
- I'm not, uh... Nothing.


00:28:21.989 --> 00:28:25.513
Paige and I had a fight,
and I spent the night here. So...


00:28:27.428 --> 00:28:29.872
Oh, my God!


00:28:30.028 --> 00:28:31.632
Hey, Nina.


00:28:31.787 --> 00:28:33.228
- What are you...
- Oh, my God!


00:28:33.388 --> 00:28:34.828
Cathy! Slow down.


00:28:34.988 --> 00:28:38.195
Slow down? I can read
an ice bucket, David.


00:28:38.348 --> 00:28:40.389
- Cathy.
- Oh, my God!


00:28:40.547 --> 00:28:43.395
I'm gonna throw up!


00:28:48.506 --> 00:28:51.027
- Jesus, David!
- Paige, listen to me.


00:28:51.187 --> 00:28:53.107
Just tell me how long
it's been going on.


00:28:53.267 --> 00:28:55.427
We kissed. That's it.


00:28:55.587 --> 00:28:58.031
Then what the hell were you
doing in a goddamn motel room?


00:28:58.186 --> 00:28:59.834
This...


00:29:01.586 --> 00:29:04.106
I'm sorry.
The whole thing was wrong.


00:29:04.266 --> 00:29:05.587
But let's be honest.


00:29:05.746 --> 00:29:07.830
Things have not been good
between us for a long time.


00:29:07.985 --> 00:29:09.469
Oh, God, don't do that.


00:29:09.625 --> 00:29:12.025
Don't apologise and then
blame me in the same sentence.


00:29:12.186 --> 00:29:14.194
Come on, Paige.
You're not happy either.


00:29:14.345 --> 00:29:16.746
It's not about
being happy, David!


00:29:16.905 --> 00:29:18.825
Well, then, what is it?


00:29:38.384 --> 00:29:40.152
Jesus, say something already.


00:29:40.304 --> 00:29:42.268
I will say something
when I want.


00:29:42.423 --> 00:29:44.824
You don't get to decide
when I say something. I decide!


00:29:44.984 --> 00:29:47.428
- Then decide already!
- I'll decide.


00:29:47.584 --> 00:29:50.868
You have caused
some serious trouble


00:29:51.024 --> 00:29:52.311
in the past, young lady.


00:29:52.463 --> 00:29:53.871
Don't you
roll your eyes at me.


00:29:54.023 --> 00:29:55.987
I'm sorry, it doesn't work
when you try to play


00:29:56.143 --> 00:29:57.867
the stern father - it looks like
you're pretending.


00:29:58.023 --> 00:30:00.107
Your father is not pretending!
We are furious!


00:30:00.262 --> 00:30:01.670
I'm not pretending.


00:30:01.823 --> 00:30:03.383
David and I,
we like each other.


00:30:03.542 --> 00:30:05.790
- Oh, my God.
- We've always been close.


00:30:05.942 --> 00:30:07.983
It's not like we planned this.
It just happened.


00:30:08.142 --> 00:30:09.747
- You like each other?
- Yeah.


00:30:09.902 --> 00:30:11.223
- Oh, my God.
- Oh, my God!


00:30:11.382 --> 00:30:13.902
I know what this is -
this is some sick revenge


