00:45:03.729 --> 00:45:06.009
he went online and found
a pick-up ultimate frisbee game


00:45:06.168 --> 00:45:07.532
in Paramus.


00:45:07.688 --> 00:45:10.732
Hey, guys! You, uh...
you got room for one more?


00:45:10.888 --> 00:45:12.972
No daylight. No daylight.


00:45:13.128 --> 00:45:17.928
So it was really Jared Kass
and I, and Joel Silver...


00:45:18.088 --> 00:45:19.768
Joel Silver,
the movie producer?


00:45:19.928 --> 00:45:21.172
Yeah. Yeah.


00:45:22.248 --> 00:45:23.731
My mother
had been making herself


00:45:23.887 --> 00:45:25.568
mysteriously unavailable.


00:45:26.727 --> 00:45:28.931
But, as all our neighbours
discovered...


00:45:30.527 --> 00:45:33.692
...she hadn't completely lost sight
of the Christmas spirit.


00:45:38.887 --> 00:45:40.295
Terry!


00:45:40.446 --> 00:45:42.126
Everything was changing.


00:45:42.287 --> 00:45:43.607
Terry!


00:45:43.766 --> 00:45:45.371
No-one even recognised
each other anymore.


00:45:48.206 --> 00:45:50.967
- Smoothie?
- Oh, good God.


00:45:54.046 --> 00:45:56.086
Very good.


00:45:56.246 --> 00:45:58.329
Now kiss the chef.


00:46:10.125 --> 00:46:12.133
Maybe they are
really in love.


00:46:12.285 --> 00:46:13.605
You said it doesn't last.


00:46:13.764 --> 00:46:16.045
You said that the grasses only
wanted the cows for their money.


00:46:16.205 --> 00:46:17.765
Usually that is the case,
but not always.


00:46:17.924 --> 00:46:19.932
- Your dad is pretty cute.
- Don't be gross, OK?


00:46:20.084 --> 00:46:21.928
Just because you haven't gotten
laid in, like, three weeks.


00:46:22.084 --> 00:46:24.048
Perhaps your problem is
more with Nina than your father.


00:46:24.204 --> 00:46:25.971
Oh, is that so, Henry?
Why is that?


00:46:26.124 --> 00:46:27.444
Because maybe
you are jealous,


00:46:27.603 --> 00:46:30.844
because she has travelled
many places and has lived,


00:46:31.004 --> 00:46:33.765
because she takes chances.


00:46:33.923 --> 00:46:35.244
No. You know what?


00:46:35.404 --> 00:46:36.931
You, my friend,
have breathed in


00:46:37.083 --> 00:46:38.927
a little too much
of this cheap pine wax, OK?


00:46:39.083 --> 00:46:41.964
'Cause she's a selfish skank.
And he's selfish too.


00:46:42.123 --> 00:46:44.404
Yeah, but if he
really is happier with her


00:46:44.563 --> 00:46:45.927
and you make him stop,


00:46:46.083 --> 00:46:47.643
then you're the one
who's being selfish.


00:46:49.483 --> 00:46:51.163
That is maybe
the most intelligent thing


00:46:51.322 --> 00:46:52.762
you have ever said.


00:47:08.401 --> 00:47:10.169
Hey.


00:47:10.321 --> 00:47:13.169
What is
Barnyard International?


00:47:13.321 --> 00:47:16.322
Well, um... See those presents
you got at babyGap?


00:47:16.481 --> 00:47:18.609
Instead of giving those
to a baby


00:47:18.760 --> 00:47:20.321
who might already
have lots of clothes,


00:47:20.481 --> 00:47:22.401
why not help a baby
who doesn't have any food?


00:47:22.561 --> 00:47:23.881
They're not for a baby.


00:47:24.040 --> 00:47:25.481
They're for my husband's
new girlfriend.


00:47:27.600 --> 00:47:29.084
Here's some pamphlets.


00:47:31.520 --> 00:47:33.964
"One goat
can provide a family


00:47:34.119 --> 00:47:36.247
"with enough milk
for an entire year."


00:47:38.040 --> 00:47:40.168
It's like the Christmas gift
that keeps giving.


00:47:40.319 --> 00:47:41.879
Yeah. It is.


00:47:42.040 --> 00:47:43.960
That's good. Can I use that?


00:47:44.119 --> 00:47:46.563
Sure.


00:47:53.919 --> 00:47:56.166
Oh, yes! Oh! Oh!


00:48:03.878 --> 00:48:06.878
There are gift receipts inside,
if anyone wants to return them.


00:48:10.518 --> 00:48:12.242
I think after Christmas Eve,


00:48:12.397 --> 00:48:14.842
we should demand
that Paige have dinner with us.


00:48:17.797 --> 00:48:19.477
What are you doing?


00:48:19.637 --> 00:48:21.284
Come here.


00:48:23.437 --> 00:48:25.837
- I have toothpaste in my mouth.
- I don't care.


00:48:31.036 --> 00:48:32.760
Come here.


00:48:43.436 --> 00:48:46.480
OK. Thank you
for dropping me off.


00:48:46.636 --> 00:48:48.677
I got you these.


00:48:53.755 --> 00:48:55.555
Chef's clogs.


00:48:55.715 --> 00:48:57.602
You said after working last night,
your feet hurt, so...


00:48:57.754 --> 00:48:59.434
You're so sweet.


00:49:08.074 --> 00:49:09.918
OK. You're gonna
make me late.


00:49:10.074 --> 00:49:11.874
Whoo!


00:49:21.633 --> 00:49:22.953
- That was fast.
- Yeah.


00:49:23.114 --> 00:49:25.274
Um...


00:49:25.433 --> 00:49:26.917
What?


00:49:29.073 --> 00:49:30.393
Nothing.


00:49:30.552 --> 00:49:31.873
What's up?


00:49:32.033 --> 00:49:33.354
Nothing.


00:49:33.513 --> 00:49:35.117
Come on.
Tell me what's wrong.


00:49:37.032 --> 00:49:39.313
- I...
- I love you, Nina.


00:49:41.272 --> 00:49:44.753
You shit. You suck.
I wanted to say it first.


00:49:46.512 --> 00:49:49.273
Well, now I'm not saying it.
You blew it, buddy.


00:49:51.271 --> 00:49:53.475
I'm just kidding.
I love you too.


00:49:58.391 --> 00:50:01.031
You guys were married
for 28 years.


00:50:01.191 --> 00:50:03.439
If anyone should call,
it should be him.


00:50:03.590 --> 00:50:05.631
- Do you have any perfume?
- No.


00:50:05.790 --> 00:50:08.475
What?! Where are you
even going?


00:50:08.631 --> 00:50:11.031
Well, I read about
a late-evening cabaret show


00:50:11.190 --> 00:50:12.674
that begins at 9:30.


00:50:12.830 --> 00:50:15.078
- I'm taking myself out.
- Cabaret?


00:50:15.231 --> 00:50:17.359
Am I the only one
who's dealing with this?


00:50:17.510 --> 00:50:21.111
I mean, don't you
want to come back home?


00:50:23.069 --> 00:50:24.510
I'm not sure.


00:50:24.670 --> 00:50:27.190
I'm having a good time
for once.


00:50:27.349 --> 00:50:31.277
I'd like to see you
do the same.


00:50:34.869 --> 00:50:36.396
Let's go, guys!
Pick up the pace!


00:50:36.549 --> 00:50:38.229
Hey, Mondo!
Where's my rigatoni? Let's go!


00:50:38.389 --> 00:50:39.873
Bring it up, parmigiana.


00:50:40.029 --> 00:50:41.829
Nina! Plate 27!


00:50:41.988 --> 00:50:43.352
Alright, guys-


00:50:43.508 --> 00:50:45.832
On 24, I got a mahi mahi
and a chicken parmigiana.


00:50:45.988 --> 00:50:47.875
Thanks for sending her to me.
She's a good worker.


00:50:48.028 --> 00:50:49.436
- Well, that's great.
- Chef likes her.


00:50:49.588 --> 00:50:52.753
Haven't seen you and Paige
for a while. It's good to see you.


00:50:52.908 --> 00:50:55.353
- Enjoy.
- Thanks.


00:51:24.266 --> 00:51:27.190
- Done with your appetiser, sir?
- Sorry?


00:51:27.346 --> 00:51:28.874
Done with
your appetiser, sir?


00:51:29.025 --> 00:51:30.989
Yeah. That... Yeah.
That's great. Thanks.


00:51:35.706 --> 00:51:37.233
Hello.


00:51:38.545 --> 00:51:40.073
Hi, Paige.


00:51:42.065 --> 00:51:44.552
Nice move
on the Christmas card.


00:51:44.705 --> 00:51:46.352
Thank you.


00:51:47.385 --> 00:51:50.506
- Dining alone?
- Uh, yeah. I guess.


00:51:51.824 --> 00:51:53.668
So how are you doing?
Is everything...


00:51:53.825 --> 00:51:55.625
Sit down. Don't have to
make this uncomfortable.


00:51:55.784 --> 00:51:57.267
Just...


00:51:59.904 --> 00:52:02.152
Plus, you know
how I hate pleasantries.


00:52:03.664 --> 00:52:05.748
What about you?


00:52:05.903 --> 00:52:07.911
You look happy.


00:52:09.304 --> 00:52:10.864
Things are OK.
You know, I'm...


00:52:11.023 --> 00:52:13.468
If you're happy,
you can say so.


00:52:13.623 --> 00:52:15.390
You don't need
to spare my feelings.


00:52:15.543 --> 00:52:19.427
Just...be genuine,
David, please.


00:52:19.583 --> 00:52:21.187
Please.


00:52:23.583 --> 00:52:25.743
Yes. I'm happy-


00:52:29.142 --> 00:52:30.702
Thank you.


00:52:30.862 --> 00:52:32.422
Yeah.


00:52:33.822 --> 00:52:35.742
Look, I know
there's nothing I can say...


00:52:35.902 --> 00:52:37.310
Then don't try.


00:52:37.461 --> 00:52:39.261
Paige, stop. Please.


00:52:39.421 --> 00:52:41.669
This is exactly
how we got to this.


00:52:43.062 --> 00:52:47.503
OK, not exactly.
It's partly.


00:52:47.661 --> 00:52:50.509
We stopped talking
to each other.


00:52:52.861 --> 00:52:55.425
I used to love who I was
around you.


00:52:55.580 --> 00:52:58.308
What happened to us?


00:52:59.860 --> 00:53:02.348
We used to have fun.
Remember that?


00:53:04.300 --> 00:53:06.821
We used to laugh.
God, you were so funny.


00:53:06.980 --> 00:53:08.627
I'm still funny.


00:53:08.780 --> 00:53:10.864
I'm... Ask them.


00:53:32.819 --> 00:53:34.586
Shelly just fired me!


00:53:34.739 --> 00:53:36.266
Hey, hey.


00:53:36.418 --> 00:53:39.745
- What happened?
- Oh! This is fucking bullshit!


00:53:39.898 --> 00:53:42.462
- What? Why?
- Because he's not an idiot.


00:53:42.618 --> 00:53:45.378
He saw you and Paige, and he
saw me, and he figured it out.


00:53:45.538 --> 00:53:47.861
He said he didn't want
to be in the middle of it.


00:53:48.018 --> 00:53:50.026
And I was good at that job!


00:53:50.177 --> 00:53:52.141
Why...


00:53:52.298 --> 00:53:54.578
Why were you talking to her?


00:53:54.737 --> 00:53:56.417
She came into the restaurant.


00:53:56.576 --> 00:53:59.337
What do you expect me to do?


00:53:59.497 --> 00:54:01.820
I saw you sitting with her,
and I just thought...


00:54:04.377 --> 00:54:05.697
Thought what?


00:54:05.857 --> 00:54:07.624
I don't know.


00:54:10.096 --> 00:54:11.984
You looked normal together.


00:54:19.215 --> 00:54:21.823
Can we please get out of here?


00:54:29.894 --> 00:54:31.258
# I really can't stay


00:54:31.414 --> 00:54:33.214
# But, baby,
it's cold outside


00:54:33.375 --> 00:54:36.255
- # I've got to go away
- # But, baby, it's cold outside


00:54:36.415 --> 00:54:38.019
# This evening has been...


00:54:38.174 --> 00:54:39.702
# Been hoping
that you drop in


00:54:39.854 --> 00:54:41.218
# So very nice


00:54:41.374 --> 00:54:44.418
# I'll hold your hands
They're just like ice


00:54:44.574 --> 00:54:46.374
# My mother
will start to worry... I


00:54:46.534 --> 00:54:48.301
Hi. Mrs Ostroff'?


00:54:48.454 --> 00:54:50.101
We've never met.


00:54:50.254 --> 00:54:52.382
But I'm Ethan.


00:54:57.174 --> 00:54:58.898
You're our leader.
You can't quit!


00:54:59.053 --> 00:55:02.294
Christmas Eve is in, like,
six days. They're counting on us.


00:55:02.453 --> 00:55:06.621
Try and calm down. Calm down.


00:55:06.773 --> 00:55:09.654
Calm down. Order!


00:55:09.812 --> 00:55:11.699
I know you're upset.


00:55:11.853 --> 00:55:15.421
But you're all
dedicated and talented singers.


00:55:16.892 --> 00:55:18.213
Marcus will take over
as leader.


00:55:18.372 --> 00:55:20.696
- What?!
- Marcus?


00:55:20.852 --> 00:55:22.816
- Why are you even doing this?
- Yeah.


00:55:22.971 --> 00:55:26.615
Well, I believe these pamphlets
should explain everything.


00:55:26.772 --> 00:55:29.456
Each cow or goat
will allow its recipient


00:55:29.611 --> 00:55:32.219
independence
and self-sufficiency


00:55:32.371 --> 00:55:34.652
for years to come.


00:55:35.651 --> 00:55:37.855
And that's pretty great,
isn't it?


00:55:39.171 --> 00:55:42.019
Shelly, this has
nothing to do with you.


00:55:42.170 --> 00:55:44.014
No, I know it's complicated.


00:55:44.171 --> 00:55:46.255
No. I understand.


00:55:47.690 --> 00:55:49.458
Thanks for calling back.


00:55:52.290 --> 00:55:53.611
Told you.


00:55:53.770 --> 00:55:55.494
He'll write you
a reference, but...


00:55:55.650 --> 00:55:57.254
Yeah. He doesn't
want to get involved.


00:55:57.409 --> 00:56:00.891
This isn't gonna work.
I need to find another job.


00:56:01.050 --> 00:56:02.730
I can't stay at Meredith's
rent-free.


00:56:02.889 --> 00:56:04.210
I know.


00:56:04.370 --> 00:56:05.690
And I can't stay here,


00:56:05.849 --> 00:56:07.257
across the street
from my parents.


00:56:07.409 --> 00:56:10.170
- I love you. But...
- What the fuck?


00:56:10.329 --> 00:56:13.733
- Ethan?
- What the hell is going on?


00:56:13.889 --> 00:56:16.977
- What are you doing here?
- Ethan? Like, Ethan Ethan?


00:56:17.129 --> 00:56:20.010
- How did you get in here?
- Your mom gave me the keys.


00:56:20.168 --> 00:56:21.816
She told me
to let myself in,


00:56:21.968 --> 00:56:23.496
like you might not
hear the bell.


00:56:23.648 --> 00:56:26.168
Look, Ethan, I'm sorry, but I'm
gonna have to ask you to leave.


00:56:26.328 --> 00:56:29.732
You can ask, but I'm not gonna.
Who is this?


00:56:29.887 --> 00:56:31.775
Ethan, this is David -
David and Paige,


00:56:31.928 --> 00:56:33.892
my parents' best friends
from across the street.


00:56:35.127 --> 00:56:36.687
Why are you telling
your parents' friend


00:56:36.848 --> 00:56:38.168
that you love him?


00:56:38.327 --> 00:56:40.575
The door's open.
What's going on?


00:56:40.727 --> 00:56:42.975
Nina, I need to talk to you.


00:56:43.127 --> 00:56:45.211
Can we go somewhere
for, like, five minutes?


00:56:45.367 --> 00:56:47.047
Ethan!
I think you should leave.


00:56:47.207 --> 00:56:50.055
- Ethan Ethan?
- Yes! Just five minutes!


00:56:50.206 --> 00:56:52.126
She said no, Ethan.


00:56:52.286 --> 00:56:54.534
I'm gonna ask you one more time
to get out of here.


00:56:54.687 --> 00:56:59.335
And if I don't, Pops,
what are you gonna do about it?


00:56:59.486 --> 00:57:00.446
Arggh!


00:57:00.605 --> 00:57:02.013
'Dad!
Hey!


00:57:02.166 --> 00:57:03.006
- David!
- Dad!


00:57:03.166 --> 00:57:04.770
Get off me!


00:57:06.206 --> 00:57:08.454
# Your eyes
are like starlight now


00:57:08.605 --> 00:57:10.133
# To break this spell


00:57:10.285 --> 00:57:13.166
# I'll take your hat
Your hair looks swell... #


00:57:13.325 --> 00:57:15.125
Why don't you go fuck...


00:57:15.285 --> 00:57:18.012
- What?
- Nothing.


00:57:18.164 --> 00:57:19.769
Its OK.


00:57:22.444 --> 00:57:26.645
# Baby,
it's cold outside. #


00:57:36.564 --> 00:57:40.492
Yes, I cheated on you.
And for that, I am deeply sorry.


00:57:40.644 --> 00:57:43.732
But here's the thing.
I'm a sabotager.


00:57:43.883 --> 00:57:47.484
See, any time
anything good happens to me,


00:57:47.643 --> 00:57:49.487
I...I...I just try
and ruin it, you know,


00:57:49.643 --> 00:57:51.203
because I get scared.


00:57:51.363 --> 00:57:55.051
Now, things with us
were really...real.


00:57:55.202 --> 00:57:57.810
But I didn't feel like
I deserved you,


00:57:57.962 --> 00:58:01.563
so I became the sabotager
and, like, destroyed it.


00:58:01.722 --> 00:58:03.686
That's great, Ethan.


00:58:03.842 --> 00:58:05.926
But we can't just go on
and pretend like everything's fine


00:58:06.082 --> 00:58:07.610
because you learned
a new term about yourself.


00:58:07.762 --> 00:58:11.331
And I don't even think
'sabotager' is a word.


00:58:11.482 --> 00:58:13.369
OK. Please allow me
to finish.


00:58:13.522 --> 00:58:16.566
See, I think
you're a sabotager also.


00:58:16.721 --> 00:58:19.765
You totally pushed for us
to get married so you could, like,


00:58:19.921 --> 00:58:22.125
prove to your parents
that, you know,


00:58:22.281 --> 00:58:23.689
you were
this responsible person.


00:58:23.841 --> 00:58:27.682
But simultaneously, you were
just trying to piss them off


00:58:27.840 --> 00:58:29.760
by marrying someone like me.


00:58:29.920 --> 00:58:31.448
I've moved on.


00:58:31.601 --> 00:58:33.924
- OK? David and I...
- David and you...


00:58:34.081 --> 00:58:38.445
He's your parents' best friend.
For Christ's sakes.


00:58:38.600 --> 00:58:41.721
I mean, what... Are you gonna move
here to New Jersey?


00:58:41.880 --> 00:58:44.128
You hate it here.


00:58:46.239 --> 00:58:47.560
We're done.


00:58:47.719 --> 00:58:49.847
OK? Go home.


00:58:50.000 --> 00:58:51.527
I only bought
a one-way ticket.


00:58:54.560 --> 00:58:56.568
Well, I'm not giving up
on us, Nina!


00:58:56.719 --> 00:58:59.000
I love you too much
for that!


00:59:01.759 --> 00:59:03.919
What?


00:59:30.397 --> 00:59:31.957
What are you doing
with my bag?


00:59:32.117 --> 00:59:34.125
Huh? Nothing.
Just getting it some air.


00:59:36.357 --> 00:59:38.518
- Give me my bag.
- No.


00:59:38.677 --> 00:59:40.880
Give me my bag!


00:59:41.037 --> 00:59:44.201
- Eat me, dick slut.
- Give me my bag, Vanessa!


00:59:44.356 --> 00:59:45.839
No, Nina!


00:59:45.996 --> 00:59:47.916
- No!
- Give me my bag!


00:59:48.076 --> 00:59:51.436
- No! No!
- Give it to me!


00:59:51.596 --> 00:59:52.917
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- Give it!


00:59:53.076 --> 00:59:54.559
Oh!


01:00:29.633 --> 01:00:31.477
Oh, honey. Uh...


01:00:31.634 --> 01:00:33.314
Honey?


01:00:33.473 --> 01:00:35.393
I'm sorry, Dad.


01:00:35.553 --> 01:00:37.353
Uh...


01:00:42.912 --> 01:00:45.073
Oh...


01:00:58.072 --> 01:01:00.876
Uh, you know, leave it be.
It's a...it's a badge of honour.


01:01:01.031 --> 01:01:02.472
- You sure?
- Yeah.


01:01:02.632 --> 01:01:04.476
There's aloe on the pad
to prevent scarring.


01:01:04.631 --> 01:01:06.115
OK. Um...


01:01:06.271 --> 01:01:11.640
You know, I'm good.
I'm, uh...I'm good.


01:01:13.630 --> 01:01:15.998
I'm so sorry about
all this horrible...


01:01:17.391 --> 01:01:18.918
...stuff.


01:01:20.191 --> 01:01:21.719
I'm just...


01:01:23.071 --> 01:01:24.915
Yeah.


01:01:28.190 --> 01:01:31.878
You know,
my parents were kinda weird.


01:01:32.030 --> 01:01:34.834
That's why I'm, um...


01:01:36.190 --> 01:01:40.794
Sometimes it's really hard
to say everything you want to.


01:01:40.949 --> 01:01:42.509
You know...


01:01:43.989 --> 01:01:48.397
Your father, he loves you.


01:01:49.589 --> 01:01:52.589
Just don't let that
get confused


01:01:52.748 --> 01:01:54.996
with everything
that's happening.


01:01:59.148 --> 01:02:00.511
Life.


01:02:00.668 --> 01:02:01.988
Ooph!


